're still doing it  i can't imagine living any other way  i feel completely fulfilled  oh that's good  that's really nice  i'm working on it  [Music]  seven miles off estonia's west coast in  eastern europe lies the small island of  canoe a bucolic and serene place that  feels lost in time  home to just 400 people it functions  like one of the world's few matriarchal  societies  this is a place where women rule well  mostly everything hello welcome to  quinoa island  [Music]  my name is maria matas  i  lived almost all my life in this island  our lifestyle is different comparing the  lifestyle in the mainland many old  traditions still alive  one such tradition is that canoes men  spend months away at sea fishing for the  island  meanwhile canoes women are in charge of  leading the community and preserving its  way of life  men were always a long time away from  the island and some of the historical  reason why women become a very strong  very independent  kenyan culture is interesting because we  have still wear traditional costumes as  a everyday wearing she is making skirts  because she has five granddaughters  we have ancient folk songs still alive  and dances they have a lot of practical  skills how to  live all over the year here  yes life is more difficult here to  survive it's treasure for quinoa  islanders they all described ireland  like it's like a paradise it's the best  place in the world  [Music]  [Music]  the clothes the music  the dancing  all of it has been recognized by unesco  on its intangible cultural heritage list  the king of wedding songs and vedic  traditions are more than two thousand  years old so this is amazing why we are  in this unesco list  the same list acknowledges canoes women  as the custodians of their island's  heritage  i concern every day that our unique  culture can disappear  it's very valuable if those things still  exist and survive in the modern world  it's really  miracle  [Music]  okanoshima island is a short 12-minute 